@startuml codex-renewal
!theme plain
title Slice 1, qualification/adoption pending: Codex personal plan: one auth owner refreshes; launches use external tokens and renew within a deadline

participant "Codex app-server\n(agent OS account, no auth.json)" as A
participant "Agent-side executor\n(client of this execution's app-server)" as E
participant "Broker: auth owner\n(broker-owned home + lock)" as O

E -> O: lease.request {harness: codex_cli, channel: external-token, …}
O -> O: verify lease checks 1–7 (active UID/generation and binding,\nlease + caller chains, current revocations, source/network qualification)
O -> O: token expires within 48 h? refresh once under the lock
O --> E: payload {access_token, chatgpt_account_id, plan_type?}
E -> A: initialize (experimental capability required for external tokens)
E -> A: account/login/start {type: chatgptAuthTokens, accessToken, chatgptAccountId}
... turns ...
A -> A: model call answers 401
A -> E: account/chatgptAuthTokens/refresh (answer expected within ~10 s)
E -> O: lease.renew {lease_id, rejected_sha256} (deadline 8 s)
O -> O: check lease ownership and repeat checks 1–7
alt rejected token is still current
  O -> O: refresh once under the lock (N rejected launches → 1 refresh)
end
alt renewed within the deadline and authorisation still valid
  O -> O: after refresh, repeat authorisation under state lock\nimmediately before releasing material
  O --> E: payload {access_token, chatgpt_account_id}
  E -> E: same chatgpt_account_id as the lease?
  E --> A: refresh answer {accessToken, chatgptAccountId}
  A -> A: retry the call
else timeout or refusal
  O --> E: renew_timeout | lease_reauth_required | …
  E --> A: error answer (no late reply, no fallback login)
  A -> A: the turn fails
end
note over O: the refresh token never leaves the broker's store;\nlease_grant_revoked / lease_caller_revoked refuse renewal
note over E,A: one private app-server per execution; ephemeral storage pinned,\nno broker-mode codex exec and no shared-file/copy fallback
@enduml
